From d94e0b6a14f5f016750123fccf83c9ec13a9a3bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:28:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2320/2368] phy: core: add PHY_MODE_MIPI_CPHY

MIPI C-PHY is a three-wire, trio based physical layer that shares silicon
with D-PHY on many camera receivers but is programmed differently and has
no clock lane. Give consumers a mode value to ask a combination PHY for it,
so that a CSI-2 receiver can select the C-PHY personality the same way it
selects D-PHY today.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 46575d5a8cba1c6e45de02a126363db1fc6cd517)

diff --git a/include/linux/phy/phy.h b/include/linux/phy/phy.h
index 14b924a88411fe212d9b4b91b958ba318b93255e..3d96c036109e450cf8ed5ef077b4f2b138e09f10 100644
--- a/include/linux/phy/phy.h
+++ b/include/linux/phy/phy.h
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ enum phy_mode {
 	PHY_MODE_PCIE,
 	PHY_MODE_ETHERNET,
 	PHY_MODE_MIPI_DPHY,
+	PHY_MODE_MIPI_CPHY,
 	PHY_MODE_SATA,
 	PHY_MODE_LVDS,
 	PHY_MODE_DP,
